# MCP Server Implementation Plan for CDomain Spring Boot Application

## Executive Summary

This plan details how to implement an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for the CDomain Spring Boot 3.4.1 / Java 17 application. The MCP server will expose three domain-related tools (`check-availability`, `search-domains`, `suggest-alternatives`) that integrate with the existing `DomainService`.

---

## 1. Dependencies and Libraries

### Recommended Approach: Spring AI MCP Server Starter

Spring AI provides official MCP server support with the `spring-ai-starter-mcp-server` starters. This is the recommended approach as it integrates seamlessly with Spring Boot.

### Maven Dependencies to Add

